Subject: [PATCH] Runtime: the checkpoint's flags folded into its one compare; the plain call and the loop checkpoint in small frames

(N11f, TODO 94: the dispatcher's own cost.) Sampled in Deep Amazon (test PC, turbo, logic 240) the dispatcher was 16.8%
of the EE thread - dispatchGuestCall 9.0, dispatchGuestBranch 3.6, eeCheckpointDue 3.5 - most of it instructions every
call pays: the plain call ~80 of them, a quarter only saving and restoring the nine registers the whole dispatcher's
frame needed, the checkpoint ~25 with two flag loads and tests of their own.

- The flags folded into m_stopAtCycle (now atomic): raising the checkpoint-pending flag (or the stop) sets it to 0
  (EeScheduler::raiseCheckpoint, the flag then the 0, seq_cst - every place that set the flag, from any thread), so
  the lean checkpoint's one compare also catches them; checkpointLeanSlow tests them as before, in the same order, and
  puts the stop back once they are down (rearmStopAt). updateStopAt stores the stop, a full fence, then reads the flags
  and keeps it at 0 if one is up: a flag raised after that read writes its 0 after the store, so none is lost to a
  stop worked out again. The same answers at the same checkpoints.
- PS2X_LEAN_CHECKPOINT=0's checkpoint out of line (checkpointDueOld), so the inline one is only the lean way.
- PS2X_RAISE_LOG=1 (a measuring aid): a request made from another host thread (requestStop, requestSaveState /
  LoadState, postEvent) noted with the EE clock and the host time; the dispatcher loop logs when it is back in the loop
  after it (`[ee raise] ... after <n> EE cycles, <t> us`). Off: a constant flag tested once a dispatch.
- dispatchGuestCall = the plain call alone (round 6's plain way); everything else in dispatchGuestCallFull (out of
  line): a small frame. eeCheckpointDue (the loops' checkpoint) a leaf without a frame; PS2X_HOT_STATS's count in
  eeCheckpointDueCounted.

ps2xRuntime:
- runtime/ee_scheduler.h: checkpointDue's lean way one compare; checkpointDueOld; m_stopAtCycle atomic; updateStopAt's
  fence and flags; rearmStopAt; raiseCheckpoint; requestCheckpoint through it.
- Kernel/EeScheduler.cpp: every flag raise through raiseCheckpoint; requestStop; checkpointLeanSlow / processPendingEvents
  / reset put the stop back; PS2X_RAISE_LOG.
- ps2_runtime.h/.cpp: dispatchGuestCall / dispatchGuestCallFull; eeCheckpointDue / eeCheckpointDueCounted.

